  Hi everyone, 


One line summary of the problem:    
Blocking processes on usb stick unmount prevent suspending to ram.
Processes showing up are udisks- and hal-related.


Full description of the problem/report:
Mounting a usb stick, transferring data and then unmounting it leads to
the reported action. This is particularly annoying as it subsequently
prevents any suspend to ram. When the kernel tries to suspend to ram
it fails to suspend the reported processes and resumes immediately.
Only working solution found so far is to shutdown the system/power off.
Reported processes so far: udisk-daemon, hald-addon-store
Kernel versions tested and affected so far: 3.1.0-00009-g521, 3.1.0-00158-g4d1 


Keywords (i.e., modules, networking, kernel):
usb umount block task prevent suspend ram udisk hal


